  "title": "Macros at call sites",
  "summary": "Arguments spelled as macros hint; calls generated inside macro bodies do not",
  "prose": "An object-like macro is one written argument. A macro covering several arguments has no place to anchor a hint, and code written as a macro argument keeps its hints.",
